## Verdict

Passed. `studio/briefs/W-110.md` revision 2 clears all four MUST from the
round-2 prereview (`studio/ci/W-110-spec-2.log`) and addresses all eight
SHOULD. No finding is rebutted; one (S3) is answered with a different fix
than the one offered. Eight behaviours, unchanged in number.

## MUST

M1 — the validator now carries a **stated clause ladder** (Interfaces, four
numbered steps with explicit stop semantics and an explicit sub-order inside
step 3), and every finding count in behaviours 6 and 7 is restated against it.
7(c) says five mutations, not six, and expects one finding each — correct now
that sub-order (i) fires before (ii), since a mangled name is necessarily also
one strict match short. 6(f) expects one because step 2 stops before any entry
is read. 7(h) expects one because step 3 stops. The behaviour preamble says a
row whose prescribed count cannot be met means the ladder was built differently
and is a stop, not a test fix.

M2 — `SHOT_MAX_ENTRIES` (64) and `SHOT_MAX_BYTES` (4 MiB) join the two floors,
and `readContainedRegularFile` gains an optional `maxBytes` checked against the
`fstat` it already performs on the open fd — one line, post-open so unraceable,
every existing caller untouched. The manifest file itself is read with an 8 KiB
cap. Behaviour 7(i) fires both (65 entries with all 65 files absent, so a
ladder without the ceiling reports 65 findings instead of one; and a 4 MiB + 1
PNG) and 7(j) fires the manifest cap.

M3 — the manifest **moves out of the gate log into
`ci/shots/<opus>/manifest.txt`**. Revision 1's "last lines of the run … the
200-line tail keeps it whole" was false about the mechanism: the pipeline tails
`${r.stdout}${r.stderr}` with stderr last, so a gate command's stdout is never
the log's tail and enough stderr evicts it. Today's headroom is comfortable,
which is precisely why it was the wrong thing to build an evidence chain on —
it degrades silently as specs are added. The file is read through the
containment helper like every other `ci/` artifact, lives in the directory the
run clears, and is bound to the run by the gate's already-validated
`certifies`, `at` and `exit code: 0`. The stdout echo is kept for a human;
nothing in the rule reads it. Residual 6 states what the file does not carry
(a certificate of its own) and why that is the same trust level every `ci/*.log`
already has.

M4 — specified: `servedLines(tree)` is unchanged, `writeServedLog(root, tree,
id)` takes the record id and additionally creates `ci/shots/<id>/`, writes a
shared `VALID_SHOT_PNG` constant as two PNGs there, and writes the matching
`manifest.txt`. Each of the five call sites (W-024, W-022, W-017, W-018, W-023
— line-anchored in *Measured present state*) passes the id it already has in
scope. No fixture's gate record, state, tree or evidence path moves, so no
existing assertion about those changes.

